  <name>Scrolex</name>
  <summary>Read PDFs and ebooks horizontally</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Scrolex puts pages side by side, so you scroll left and right through a
      document instead of up and down. On a wide screen this shows several
      pages at once without wasted space.
    </p>
    <p>
      It opens PDF, EPUB, MOBI, FictionBook, XPS and comic book (CBZ) files.
    </p>
    <p>Other features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Margin cropping, to fit more content on screen</li>
      <li>Hue-preserving dark mode that stays enabled across sessions</li>
      <li>Zoom with Ctrl+scroll or touchpad pinch gestures</li>
      <li>Full text search</li>
      <li>Table of contents to jump between sections</li>
      <li>One page per scroll wheel step, or keyboard navigation</li>
      <li>Sharp rendering on HiDPI displays</li>
      <li>Runs on both Wayland and X11</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
